cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Supernova Simulation"
abstract: >-
  An interactive, physically-motivated simulation of how stars die, running entirely
  in the browser. Users pick a real star or build their own, fast-forward its
  evolution, watch the core collapse and the ejecta expand in a WebGL scene at true
  relative scale, and then observe the explosion from Earth, including light travel
  time, apparent magnitude and order-of-magnitude environmental effects. All values
  are labelled as Observed, Estimated or Simulation. Intended for education and
  outreach, not as a hydrodynamics code.
